e\": \"C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 \u00b5F/25 V\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"A 0.1uF capacitor provides roughly one tenth of the intended local bulk capacitance on the display power rail. This could reduce boost-converter or panel supply stability and increase ripple. The specification is internally muddled about C1 versus C2, so this is a lower-confidence finding.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The power, regulator, battery and EPD connectivity match the specification. The two candidate deviations are a capacitor C11 carrying an inductor footprint (electrically inert, since its net is unconnected) and C1 at 0.1uF/16V where the specification lists 1 \u00b5F/25 V. The specification is ambiguous about C1, so confidence is moderate-low.\"\n}",
